{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5949,
  "title": "Remove the colon after \"Bot said\" and \"You said\" for screen readers",
  "body": "> Fixes #4363\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed [#4363](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/issues/4363), screen readers reading \"colon\" after \"Bot said\", \"You said\" and the attachment prefixes in English, in PR [#5949](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5949), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nJAWS reads punctuation by default, so \"Bot said: Hello\" was narrated as \"Bot said colon Hello\". The English screen reader greetings (\"Bot $1 said\", \"You said\", \"Bot attached\", \"You attached\") and attachment prefixes (\"A card\", \"A file\", \"A text\") no longer end with a colon; hosts with `overrideLocalizedStrings` keep their own text.\n\n## Design\n\n- Nothing replaces the colon, as the issue expects (\"bot said hello world\") and the review of #4837 kept; the live region already puts the greeting on its own line.\n- en-US only: translations come from the localization process; \"Connectivity Status: …\" is left for #5946.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `en-US.json`: colons removed from the 7 strings, comments and JSDoc examples updated\n- `accessibility/activityGreeting.noColon.html`: scan mode greeting, arrow-key summary and live region without colons (snapshot 1)\n- 28 tests: expectations without the colon\n- 43 live region snapshots: same text without the colons, no other change\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [x] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
  "author": {
